# CPAP (E0601) for obstructive sleep apnea, initial coverage, from Medicare LCD L33718. In force as published; a plan that reads a rule
# differently overrides it in the console. Every clause is quoted from library/sources/L33718-E0601.txt.
#
# Drafted by machine (library/drafts/cpap_osa.machine.vaglio), then corrected by hand: the machine draft passed every
# gate but required a symptom or comorbidity for every sleep test, where the LCD requires one only when the AHI or RDI
# is 5 to 14. Here an AHI or RDI of 15 or more qualifies by itself, and 5 to 14 qualifies with either kind of support.
# Questions only: the LCD names no codes for the sleep test's result or the symptoms, and a code this policy does not
# hold would match nothing.
policy cpap_osa
  title "CPAP device (E0601) for obstructive sleep apnea, initial coverage"
  version 0.1.0
  source "Medicare LCD L33718, Positive Airway Pressure (PAP) Devices for the Treatment of Obstructive Sleep Apnea: initial coverage of E0601"
  authority lcd
  lines medicare-advantage medicare
  questionnaire https://vaglio.example/Questionnaire/cpap-osa
  service hcpcs E0601

evidence clinical_evaluation
  text "An in-person clinical evaluation for obstructive sleep apnea before the sleep test"
  clause "The beneficiary has an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner prior to the sleep test to assess the beneficiary for obstructive sleep apnea."
  find question clinical-evaluation

evidence ahi_15_or_more
  text "A sleep test with an AHI or RDI of 15 or more events per hour, with at least 30 events"
  clause "The apnea-hypopnea index (AHI) or Respiratory Disturbance Index (RDI) is greater than or equal to 15 events per hour with a minimum of 30 events; or,"
  find question ahi-15-or-more

evidence ahi_5_to_14
  text "A sleep test with an AHI or RDI of 5 to 14 events per hour, with at least 10 events"
  clause "The AHI or RDI is greater than or equal to 5 and less than or equal to 14 events per hour with a minimum of 10 events and documentation of:"
  find question ahi-5-to-14

evidence symptoms
  text "Documented excessive daytime sleepiness, impaired cognition, mood disorders or insomnia"
  clause "Excessive daytime sleepiness, impaired cognition, mood disorders, or insomnia; or,"
  find question osa-symptoms

evidence comorbidity
  text "Documented hypertension, ischemic heart disease or history of stroke"
  clause "Hypertension, ischemic heart disease, or history of stroke."
  find question osa-comorbidity

evidence device_instruction
  text "Instruction from the supplier in the proper use and care of the device"
  clause "The beneficiary and/or their caregiver has received instruction from the supplier of the device in the proper use and care of the equipment."
  find question device-instruction

criterion no_clinical_evaluation
  text "No in-person clinical evaluation before the sleep test is documented."
  clause "The beneficiary has an in-person clinical evaluation by the treating practitioner prior to the sleep test to assess the beneficiary for obstructive sleep apnea."
  defeated by clinical_evaluation

criterion not_mild_range
  text "The sleep test's AHI or RDI is not shown to be 5 to 14."
  clause "The AHI or RDI is greater than or equal to 5 and less than or equal to 14 events per hour with a minimum of 10 events and documentation of:"
  defeated by ahi_5_to_14

criterion mild_range_unsupported
  text "Neither the symptoms nor the conditions an AHI or RDI of 5 to 14 needs are documented."
  clause "The AHI or RDI is greater than or equal to 5 and less than or equal to 14 events per hour with a minimum of 10 events and documentation of:"
  defeated by symptoms comorbidity

criterion mild_osa_qualifies
  text "An AHI or RDI of 5 to 14 with documented symptoms or conditions."
  clause "The AHI or RDI is greater than or equal to 5 and less than or equal to 14 events per hour with a minimum of 10 events and documentation of:"
  defeated by not_mild_range mild_range_unsupported

criterion no_qualifying_sleep_test
  text "No sleep test meets either criterion."
  clause "The beneficiary has a sleep test (as defined below) that meets either of the following criteria (1 or 2):"
  defeated by ahi_15_or_more mild_osa_qualifies

criterion no_device_instruction
  text "Instruction in the use and care of the device is not documented."
  clause "The beneficiary and/or their caregiver has received instruction from the supplier of the device in the proper use and care of the equipment."
  defeated by device_instruction

decision approve approves
  text "Approve the E0601 device."
  clause "An E0601 device is covered for the treatment of obstructive sleep apnea (OSA) if criteria A – C are met:"
  defeated by no_clinical_evaluation no_qualifying_sleep_test no_device_instruction

decision deny_no_evaluation denies
  text "Deny: no in-person clinical evaluation before the sleep test."
  clause "If a claim for an E0601 is submitted and all of the criteria above have not been met, it will be denied as not reasonable and necessary."
  defeated by clinical_evaluation

decision deny_no_qualifying_test denies
  text "Deny: no sleep test meets either criterion."
  clause "If a claim for an E0601 is submitted and all of the criteria above have not been met, it will be denied as not reasonable and necessary."
  defeated by ahi_15_or_more mild_osa_qualifies

decision deny_no_instruction denies
  text "Deny: instruction in the use and care of the device is not documented."
  clause "If a claim for an E0601 is submitted and all of the criteria above have not been met, it will be denied as not reasonable and necessary."
  defeated by device_instruction
